---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const research = (await getCollection('work')).filter(p=>['human-ai-collaboration','synthetic-pilot-lab','protein-language-models'].includes(p.id)).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
---
<Layout title="Research — Ashmit Mukherjee" description="Computational social science, experimental systems, and machine learning. Research experience and manuscript by Ashmit Mukherjee at NYU Abu Dhabi.">
  <div class="container research-page">
    <header class="page-intro"><h1>Research</h1><p>I am interested in using data, statistics, and computing to study social, economic, and historical questions. My current projects concern human–AI interaction and experimental methods. At the eBRAIN Lab, I work on protein-model adaptation and test how results change across seeds and model sizes.</p><div class="inline-links"><a class="text-link" href="/work/">All projects ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="mailto:asm8879@nyu.edu">Get in touch ↗</a></div></header>
    <section class="section research-projects" aria-labelledby="current-heading"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="current-heading">Research projects</h2></div>{research.map((p,i)=><article class="project-row"><span class="project-number">0{i+1}</span><div><p class="eyebrow">{p.data.status}</p><h3><a href={`/work/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a></h3><p>{p.data.summary}</p><p class="research-role">{p.data.role} · {p.data.organization}</p>{p.id==='protein-language-models' && <div class="manuscript-note" id="manuscript"><p><strong>Bio-LoRA: Biological Priors as Inductive Bias for Low-Rank Adaptation.</strong> Co-first author. Unpublished manuscript, 2026.</p></div>}</div><a class="row-link" href={`/work/${p.id}/`} aria-label={`Read ${p.data.title}`}>↗</a></article>)}</section>
    <section class="section split"><div><h2>Related work</h2></div><div><p>Hinglish named-entity recognition gave me experience with multilingual training pipelines and the interpretation of results from different test settings. FieldLens explores another evaluation problem: connecting a model's answer to source records while preserving uncertainty and handling failures.</p><div class="inline-links"><a class="text-link" href="/work/hinglish-ner/">Hinglish NER ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/work/fieldlens/">FieldLens ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/work/">All work ↗</a></div></div></section>
    <p class="content-date">Research status reviewed 17 October 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
